  "snippet": "increase from late May into June. Those traveling during this period will need rain gear. Next, let's look at detailed information by region around Tokyo. Around Tokyo. SaiTama, Kanagawa,Chiba. In the Tokyo area, may temperatures range from about 13°C to 22°C with more warm days than April. The daytime is very comfortable. On the other hand, it can feel a bit\nchilly in the mornings and evenings. The basic style I recommend is layering a cardigan over a thin base layer. By the way, in 2025, there were days in late [...] close to summer with temperatures from 17°C to 30°C. Note that the clothing needed is different from the Tokyo area. In late May 2025, some days reached 34°C. Okinawa typically enters the rainy season in early May, characterized by more rain and humid days. Have an umbrella or raincoat ready because of the high humidity. Breathable fabrics are recommended. On sunny days, you'll be comfortable [...] as it can drop to near ten degrees Celsius at night. Heavy coats aren't necessary, but carrying a light outer like a mountain parka or cardigan is recommended. Rain is infrequent in this area in May, but a foldable"
