{
  "title": "Tokyo Weather in May 2026 - Japan - Asia Odyssey Travel",
  "url": "https://www.asiaodysseytravel.com/japan/tokyo-may-weather.html",
  "snippet": "Tokyo Tower Panoramic View\n\nTokyo Tower Panoramic View\n\n Average Daily Temperature: 16-23°C (61-73°F)\n Daytime Highs: 23-25°C (73-77°F)\n Nighttime Lows: 14-16°C (57-61°F)\n Rainfall: 132mm over 8-10 days (manageable)\n Humidity: Starting to rise (66%) but not oppressive\n Comparison: Similar to San Francisco summer or Mediterranean spring\n Real feel: Like perfect spring anywhere in the world\n\nThis temperature range is Tokyo's sweet spot. You're past April's mood swings when one day might be 10°C and the next 20°C. May brings stability. The weather becomes predictable enough to plan outdoor activities without constantly checking forecasts.\n\n### Tokyo Weather Late May: Why May 20-31 is the Sweet Spot [...] | Date | Event | Location | What to Expect |\n ---  --- |\n| Apr 29 - May 6 | Golden Week | Citywide | Extreme crowds, high prices |\n| May 3-5 | Children's Day Festival | Tokyo Skytree | 1,500 carp streamers |\n| May 5 | Kachiya Matsuri | Kameido | Samurai parade |\n| May 10-11 | Kanda Matsuri | Akihabara area | Historic procession |\n| May 10-24 | Sumo Tournament | Ryogoku | 15-day tournament |\n| May 16-18 | Sanja Matsuri | Asakusa | 2 million visitors |\n| May 20 | Tokyo Port Festival | Tokyo Bay | Free port tours |\n| Late May | Firefly Viewing | Hotel Chinzanso | Evening illumination |\n\nNote: Book accommodations 3-6 months ahead for Golden Week, 1-2 months for other May dates. [...] The weather was consistently bright and comfortably warm, making it ideal for exploring neighborhoods like Shibuya or Yanaka with just a light layer. The summer humidity hadn't arrived yet, and the parks were a vibrant green.\n\nWhile the Golden Week holiday at the start of the month was incredibly busy, the weeks that followed offered a fantastic trade-off: beautiful spring conditions without the shoulder-to-shoulder crowds of the sakura season.\n\nSo, how can you capture that same perfect experience in May 2026? This Tokyo May guide breaks down everything you need to know.\n\n## Content Preview"
}
